# Hub capacity

The user requested capacity-first maintenance on 2026-10-29. Large image work
is occasional; optimize the current workflow before adding new infrastructure.

- Before publishing, distinguish the Git frontend from the independent CLI
  executor. Confirm each project's plan, deployment method, Root/Build/Output
  and current limits when accessible; explicitly report any missing access.
- For new/replaced art, measure file count, total added bytes, largest files
  and the resulting output. Use display-appropriate dimensions and compatible
  optimized formats. Keep generation originals, ZIPs and QA recordings outside
  production output; preserve all required final artwork and licenses.
- Batch image creation, compression and review, then consolidate validated
  changes into as few releases as practical. Splitting one final site across
  repeated full deployments does not shrink it and may retain more output.
- Check actual team Usage for Deployment Storage and Functions Storage,
  plus transfer/image-processing usage when relevant. Do not substitute source
  folder size, public URL totals or size multiplied by deployment count.
- Leave headroom below the verified applicable limit. Aim for at least 20%
  remaining where measurable; this is an internal goal, NOT a Vercel email
  threshold. Never claim capacity is safe when current Usage is inaccessible.
- If a verified proposed release would exceed a limit, optimize or reduce
  unnecessary output first and report unresolved capacity before publishing.
  Do not silently remove games, valid banks, required images or runtime files.
- Verify each exclusion against actual deployment output and game/backend
  references. A 404 does not prove packaging exclusion. Avoid blanket prompt,
  Markdown, runtime or old-art exclusions: some are active dependencies.
- Keep upload caps, retained storage, traffic and spend alerts separate.
  Notification thresholds vary by metric, plan and recipient preferences;
  never invent a universal project-MB email trigger. Recheck official docs.
- Do not delete history, change cloud retention, disable alerts, upgrade the
  plan or move assets to paid storage without explicit task authorization.
- Report capacity before/after and verified limits for asset-heavy releases;
  optimize only what is needed and preserve unrelated games and service routes.

